# Server-function authorization (ADR-0002)

Route guards (`_authenticated`, `beforeLoad` redirects) are **UX only**. Server
functions are RPC endpoints reachable without matching a route.

## Rule

Every server function that touches user data MUST:

1. Obtain `userId` from `authed` (`src/lib/server-auth.ts`)
2. Constrain every query/mutation with that `userId`

`authed` authenticates. It does **not** authorize rows — put `eq(table.userId, userId)`
(or equivalent) in the same expression that reads or writes.

## Pattern

Put auth in the **handler** module; keep `createServerFn` wiring thin (ADR-0005):

```ts
// items.handlers.ts
export const findItem = authed(
  async ({ data, userId }: { data: { id: number }; userId: string }) =>
    await db
      .select()
      .from(items)
      .where(and(eq(items.id, data.id), eq(items.userId, userId))),
)

// items.ts
export const getItem = createServerFn({ method: 'GET' })
  .validator(itemIdSchema)
  .handler(findItem)
```

## Do not

```ts
// ❌ BAD — auth() inlined, easy to omit; no row scope
.handler(async ({ data }) => {
  const { userId } = await auth()
  if (!userId) throw new Error('Unauthorized')
  return db.select().from(items).where(eq(items.id, data.id))
})

// ❌ BAD — trusting _authenticated / beforeLoad as the security boundary
```

Public demos (e.g. `/demo/drizzle` todos under `src/lib/demo/`) may omit `authed`
only when the table has no owner and the data is intentionally shared. Product
features must not copy that shortcut.

See `docs/adr/0002-enforce-authorization-in-server-functions.md` and
`.cursor/rules/server-functions-data-access.mdc`.
